1
00:00:01,194 --> 00:00:01,928
StreamWell.

2
00:00:01,928 --> 00:00:03,063
Check the stream.

3
00:00:03,063 --> 00:00:04,065
Check yourself.

4
00:00:05,811 --> 00:00:09,982
OneAquaHealth asks: do healthy urban streams make healthier people?

5
00:00:10,546 --> 00:00:16,053
Citizen science can watch hundreds of streams, but only about a quarter of volunteers ever come back.

6
00:00:16,623 --> 00:00:20,223
And a stream record says nothing about how the stream made anyone feel.

7
00:00:20,223 --> 00:00:22,251
The human half of One Health is missing.

8
00:00:24,026 --> 00:00:26,239
StreamWell fixes both with one idea.

9
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:30,113
Every visit becomes two health checks: the stream’s, and yours.

10
00:00:32,534 --> 00:00:33,110
Meet Ana.

11
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:39,122
After work she walks to a stream in Coimbra, one of the 106 real OneAquaHealth research sites.

12
00:00:41,681 --> 00:00:46,754
She sees today’s safe-walk advisory, and the project’s own lab health-risk score for this stream.

13
00:00:48,432 --> 00:00:52,126
First, thirty seconds: joy, calm, irritation and worry.

14
00:00:52,126 --> 00:00:56,223
The same four feelings the OneAquaHealth app already records.

15
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:58,036
StreamWell asks them twice.

16
00:01:02,944 --> 00:01:08,353
Then the official OneAquaHealth stream check, in plain words and pictures, with an honest "not sure".

17
00:01:27,854 --> 00:01:28,906
Then a second look.

18
00:01:28,906 --> 00:01:34,889
Explainable checks compare her answers with each other, with recent weather and with her photo, and say why.

19
00:01:37,829 --> 00:01:38,880
The AI suggests.

20
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:42,426
Ana decides, and her decision travels with the record.

21
00:01:49,837 --> 00:01:51,692
Two health checks, side by side.

22
00:01:51,692 --> 00:01:54,416
The stream is Good, with every point explained.

23
00:01:54,416 --> 00:01:56,967
And Ana left more restored than she arrived.

24
00:02:02,347 --> 00:02:03,601
Her data, her choice.

25
00:02:03,601 --> 00:02:06,349
Feelings stay on her phone unless she opts in.

26
00:02:08,134 --> 00:02:09,915
This is the reason to come back.

27
00:02:09,915 --> 00:02:13,311
Over weeks, her journal shows which streams restore her most.

28
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:17,547
The reward is personal insight, not points.

29
00:02:19,304 --> 00:02:22,734
Missions send volunteers to streams nobody has checked for a month.

30
00:02:24,305 --> 00:02:28,457
And a family doctor can prescribe stream walks, as a blue prescription.

31
00:02:31,264 --> 00:02:35,012
For cities: every site, with the real OneAquaHealth lab scores.

32
00:02:35,012 --> 00:02:39,474
These visits are simulated, because this paired dataset does not exist yet.

33
00:02:39,474 --> 00:02:40,961
Creating it is the point.

34
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:47,963
Healthier streams, more restored people, made measurable.

35
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:51,265
Feeling unsafe, smells and litter cost the most.

36
00:02:51,265 --> 00:02:53,316
Each becomes an action for the city.

37
00:02:57,868 --> 00:03:02,359
If a storm hits tonight, risky streams turn red, with safer ones nearby.

38
00:03:04,161 --> 00:03:10,161
Everything is HL7 FHIR on the OneAquaHealth Implementation Guide, at two privacy levels.

39
00:03:11,632 --> 00:03:13,150
Zero validation errors.

40
00:03:25,805 --> 00:03:27,233
We checked our own work.

41
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:34,134
In two hundred simulated pilots, the model found every planted effect, and a fake one only four percent of the time.

42
00:03:34,134 --> 00:03:35,681
Zero accessibility issues.

43
00:03:35,681 --> 00:03:39,310
And a pre-registered pilot, ready for one OneAquaHealth city.

44
00:03:39,876 --> 00:03:40,641
StreamWell.

45
00:03:40,641 --> 00:03:41,822
Check the stream.

46
00:03:41,822 --> 00:03:42,865
Check yourself.

47
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:43,560
Thank you.
